# Line-ending policy. The committed bytes are the convention, and `-text` is what makes a
# clone reproduce them: git performs no end-of-line conversion in either direction, on any
# platform, whatever a contributor's `core.autocrlf` happens to be set to.
#
# Every tracked text file is LF since 0.2.14, converted in one commit. Harness gate 16
# (`scripts/harness_gate.py`) fails a file that mixes the two conventions, or whose convention
# differs from its committed bytes.
* -text
